$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Deuterium Labeling Experiment. A magnetic stirring bar, 1a (121.6 mg,
0.51 mmol), 2a (105.2 mg, 1.1 mmol), NaBD3CN (162.3 mg, 4.8 mmol, 96
atom% D) and methanol (1.0 mL) were placed in a pyrex 10 mL
round-bottomed flask and irradiated by Xenon arc lamp (500 W) with
stirring for 3 h under argon. The reaction mixture was poured into water
(20 mL) and extracted with Et2O (20 mL x 3). The organic layer was washed
with brine, and dried over Na2SO4, then filtered and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
(hexane/ Et2O = 20/1) to give 3 a-d (46.6 mg).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, regioselective, Tin-Free Giese Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
