$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Synthesis of 4aa A
magnetic stirring bar, 1a (240.8 mg, 1.0 mmol), 2a (150.5 mg, 1.5 mmol),
3 (302.1 mg, 1.2 mmol), PdCl2 (9.0 mg, 0.05 mmol), LiCl (8.9 mg, 0.2
mmol), Et3N (151.0 mg, 1.5 mmol), and C6H6 (10 mL) were placed in Pyrex
vial under Ar. Then, t-BuNC (23 µL, 0.2 mmol) was added. The solution was
irradiated with Solarbox (Xe, 1000 W/m2) with violently stirring for 16
h. The reaction mixture filtered and concentrated in vacuo to give a
residue, which was subjected to silica gel column chromatography using
hexane/EtOAc = 50/1 as eluent, 4aa (131.0 mg, 0.71 mmol, 71%). ethyl
3-cyclohexylpropanoate (4aa)2 ethyl undecanoate (4ba)2 Colorless oil
(143.7 mg, 0.67 mmol, 67%). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 4.11 (t, J = 7.6
Hz, 2H), 2.29-2.45 (m, 2H), 1.64-1.55 (m, 2H), 1.30-1.22 (m, 17H), 0.87
(t, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H); 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 173.92, 60.12, 34.37,
31.82, 29.44, 29.29, 22.25, 29.12, 24.96, 22.66, 14.23, 14.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, regioselective, tin-free Giese reaction, Solarbox used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydroalkylation of alkenes using alkyl iodides and Hantzsch ester under
palladium/light system
